.TH ACCOUNT-MANAGE 8 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "Unix Administration"
.SH NAME
account-manage \- Preview or explicitly perform guarded local Linux account operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaccount-manage\fR --action ACTION --name NAME [--apply --confirm-apply]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Only local Linux accounts, not LDAP/NIS. Non-Linux operating systems (including macOS) are refused even in preview mode. Default Linux behavior is preview-only. Password locking does not revoke SSH keys or active sessions. Apply operations are not transactional and were not live-tested on system accounts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --action user-create|group-create|password-lock
Choose one local account action.
.TP
.B --name NAME
Choose the local account or group.
.TP
.B --apply --confirm-apply
Both flags, effective root privileges and a trusted Linux backend are required to modify state.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information.
.TP
.B --version
Display program version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 preview or native backend completed, 2 invalid usage, 3 unsupported/unsafe operation or backend failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
passwd(5), group(5), useradd(8), groupadd(8), usermod(8), getent(1)
.SH AUTHOR
SASD Freeware contributors.
